        "original_id": "e3e6c71a-bb5c-54a7-b678-f0835fbb560a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Manettia, Fragaria, strawberries\n- People: Saverio Manetti, Carolus Linnaeus\n- Viruses: Strawberry crinkle virus\n- Families: Rubiaceae, Rosaceae, Rhabdoviridae\n\nFacts:\n- Carolus Linnaeus named the plant genus Manettia in honour of Saverio Manetti.\n- Manettia is a genus of flowering plants in the family Rubiaceae.\n- Fragaria is a genus of flowering plants in the family Rosaceae and is commonly known as strawberries for its edible fruits.\n- Strawberry crinkle virus is a plant virus in the family Rhabdoviridae that infects plants of the genus Fragaria, commonly called strawberries.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
